  "note": "Municipal elections, 17 May 1967: four councillors for each of the three wards, all three polled. Market and Town Hall Wards are taken from the returning officer's notice of result (John Simpson, returning officer, dated 19 May 1967; Ballymena Observer, 25 May 1967, p. 9), which gives every candidate's votes; Harryville Ward is from the Belfast News-Letter, 18 May 1967, with the same figures in the notice. No party labels are printed in the notice. The unheaded second block (James B. Millar, Patrick J. Burke, David Holden, David M'Carthy elected; Robert Humphries and Robert M'Donald not elected) is printed without a ward name, so it is omitted."
